{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ARTIFACT SEARCH RESULT (2026-08-07) — the named artifacts EXIST; they were never local-only.\n\nSearched all worktrees and every branch. Both files this ticket references are present:\n* on disk at /Users/joeoakhart/impl-10ae-verifier-ctx/docs/experiments/diag_runaway_transcript.py and .../diag_runaway_matrix.py\n* in git, ADDED by commit 556708771e67ef6b73ab2c49203b657d5529611e ('Bank verifier AC verdicts; scale floor; read memo', 2026-08-06, RebarBotNava)\n\nBranch containment: 556708771e is reachable ONLY from branch impl-10ae-verifier-ctx. Verified NOT an ancestor of origin/main.\n\nSo the earlier triage's premise — 'the named artifacts do not exist on main, so the capture may have been intentionally local-only' — is wrong in its conclusion. The capture was committed, not local-only; the commit simply never landed. The disposition question is therefore not 'was this intentional?' but 'should impl-10ae-verifier-ctx's diagnostic artifacts be landed on main, or are they a working-branch aid that main does not need?'\n\nWorth noting the general hazard this exposes: a ticket citing artifacts by path is only verifiable against the branch that holds them, and a reviewer checking main will conclude they were never produced."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786097702287857001,"uuid":"9736b869-aa3b-4718-8c28-0fc124c4614d"}